 - **Speed S2-10, partial (2026-11-13, landed 2026-11-15; saves, loads and town builds with a live screen, speed audit 2 cause C7; measured on libmgba, PCSX-Redux and Flycast on `81542c47`, `61728c76`, `167c08ba`, `262bf2b7`, `6e8363ab` and the tip it landed on, `91479d4c`; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 2: S2-10", docs/PS1.md "Speed tour 2", docs/DREAMCAST.md "Speed tour 2"):** the work still runs in one tick (the sim stops for the whole job; 95% of a GBA save is the codec rebuilding every citizen's base record twice, not the flash), but the screen is alive: the core calls `plat_busy` / `plat_busy_step` (`plat_ext.h`) per citizen, per sort pass, every 32 relationships and per flash sector. GBA: a save dims the picture and shows a 144 x 30 card "Saving... / Do not switch off!", a load or a build fades to black with "Loading...", a ring of dots turns 30 times a second from the VBlank IRQ; after the job the card's rows are copied back so a held frame stays held. PS1: the loading screen follows the work, card I/O two sectors a call with a picture after each, a dot ring over long overlay reads. Dreamcast: the VMU card also covers the encode, decode and builds. Worst gap between two pictures, before -> after: GBA save 13,629 / 15,688 ms -> **50 / 50 ms**, load 7,166 / 8,539 -> **50 / 67 ms**, New story 2,310 -> **67 ms**, new island 2,210 -> 117 ms (the hub's own frames, S3-14); PS1 save 9,667 -> 367-400 ms, load 8,383 -> 767 ms, New story 2,483 -> 383 ms, new island 1,900 -> 183-200 ms; Dreamcast save 3,335 / 3,456 -> 184 / 267 ms, load 956 / 876 -> **83 / 83 ms**, builds 130 / 123 -> **100 / 100 ms**. **Not met:** no gap over ~100 ms on the PS1 (single blocking BIOS calls: the config record write, a load's directory scan, the scene enter after a build) and for Dreamcast saves (the VMU's directory and FAT writes); the GBA new island (S3-14). Same saved bytes (`test_save_golden`, the GBA flash and PS1 card images sha256-identical on `ee686c74`, `make -C dc vmu-test`); power cut